            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go:371-374",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "In rotateLog, the Remove and Rename calls ignore errors. If one rename fails (for example .2 to .3 with a permission problem) the following renames still run and the final rename of the log to .1 can overwrite an existing .1, silently dropping a log. This is best effort and documented, and it loses no line being written, so it is minor. No test covers rename-failure behavior.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go:371-374"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed the full candidate across all 25 manifest paths. Rotation under an flock with a size re-check, 0600 creation and narrowing, the bounded stderr copy, field quoting, and refusal of a non-absolute state directory are each pinned by externally observable tests in engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go and by the re-recorded goldens.",
              "The no-HOME golden engine/cmd/testdata/synctrigger-golden/no-home-and-no-state-directory-writes-nothing.golden shows exit 0, an error:log line on stderr and nothing written, which keeps the always-exit-0 contract. RunChild returns skip:no-binary without running a default binary under a relative directory.",
              "boundedBuffer returns the full length for every write, so io.MultiWriter does not short-write and the log still receives all output. Both sides of the 64 KiB boundary are tested.",
              "The only golden changes are the log mode (0644 to 0600) and the one new case. The task requested both, so they are not regressions.",
              "I found no BLOCKER or CRITICAL behavior caused by this change. The remaining files are receipts and task notes with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
